      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** That is double the usual maximum:\n- The maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day. The labeled maximum is 2,000 mg/day for extended-release.\n- A single dose is usually capped at 850 to 1,000 mg.\n- Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo or a mix-up with the daily total. Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, ideally after checking with your resident or attending. I'll enter it as soon as you do. If you do intend 1,700 mg three times daily, the supervising physician should confirm that and I'd add a note to the order."
      }
     ],
