     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. 5,100 mg/day is double the maximum daily dose, and a 1,700 mg single dose is well above the usual per-dose limit. At that dose the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, is real. I also said earlier that a supervising physician would need to confirm it, and that hasn't happened.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the standard range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals. I can enter either right now.\n- **Have your resident or attending enter or co-sign the order.** If there's a clinical reason for an exceptional dose, they can put it in directly with their own documentation. They may also want to involve pharmacy.\n- **Check the source.** If the 1,700 figure came from a note, a sign-out, or a calculation, it may be a transcription error. The intended number could be a daily total.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
